{
  "id": "archies",
  "name": "Archie's",
  "description": "Black chrome and black brand-voice text with the wordmark's sky blue (#44aaff) as the one accent; no navy, no dark blue (the owner's call, Sep 2026). In light the blue is never text on a light surface (2.5:1 on white): it is a fill with black text on it, a rule, or text on the black chrome. Keeps the neutral dark surface ramp.",
  "notes": {
    "--league-palette-accent": "Wordmark sky blue. 2.5:1 on white, so in light it is a FILL with --league-palette-on-accent (black, 8.4:1) on top, a rule, or text on the black chrome. On dark it is readable text (6.1:1 on the #262626 card).",
    "--color-primary": "Ink, not the blue: components use --color-primary as both text AND a fill under white text, and only black passes both.",
    "--league-accent-fg": "The accent as TEXT on a light surface. Shared components read var(--league-accent-fg, var(--league-accent, ...)), so a theme that leaves it unset renders what it did before.",
    "--on-league-accent": "Text ON a --league-accent fill.",
    "--color-gray-500": "~650 shared rules read these two grey steps directly as secondary text (breadcrumbs, table heads, counts); neutral, and dark enough for AA."
  },
